{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), we have essentially no information about whether the image modality contributes useful signal. The most critical structural question is whether multimodal fusion improves over the RNA-only baseline. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is a minimal, controlled extension of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder and profile setting, and adds only the image branch with the simplest fusion (concat). This directly answers 'does adding image information help?' If accuracy jumps substantially, we know to invest subsequent budget in multimodal variants (better encoders, multiprofile, weighted fusion). If it stays near 0.485, we know the image modality (at least with ResNet-50) is not the bottleneck and should pivot to improving the RNA side (multiprofile, scvi/scgpt encoders). This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-leverage design axis under a limited budget."
}

